     $ sqlite-utils insert dogs.db dogs dogs.json --truncate
 
+Extracting columns into lookup tables
+-------------------------------------
+
+The ``--extract`` option extracts a column into a separate lookup table. The
+original values are replaced by integer foreign keys, and repeated values use
+the same lookup-table row::
+
+    $ sqlite-utils insert dogs.db dogs dogs.json --extract breed
+
+This creates a ``breed`` table with ``id`` and ``value`` columns and stores the
+corresponding ``breed.id`` in the ``dogs.breed`` column. Use ``--extract`` more
+than once to extract multiple columns::
+
+    $ sqlite-utils insert dogs.db dogs dogs.json \
+        --extract breed --extract temperament
+
